.TH BLANKRES-APT-HOOK 1 "September 2026" "blankres 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blankres-apt-hook \- report failed package installs and upgrades
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blankres-apt-hook
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-dpkg-log
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-dry-run ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scans
.I /var/log/dpkg.log
for packages left in a failure state and reports them, so that a maintainer script which exits
non-zero is reported the same way a segfault is.
.PP
Installed as an apt
.B Post-Invoke
hook and run once after each apt invocation. There is no core dump for a package failure, so this
only ever performs stage-one reporting. It exits quietly and successfully whenever reporting is
disabled or the server is unreachable: breaking
.B apt install
in order to report a bug would be a worse failure than losing the report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file. Default
.IR /etc/blankres/client.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-dpkg-log " PATH"
Log to inspect. Default
.IR /var/log/dpkg.log .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the events that would be sent, and send nothing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/blankres/apt-hook.json
Timestamp of the newest failure already reported, so a failure is not re-reported on every
subsequent apt run.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blankresd (8),
.BR apt.conf (5)
